Run the packaged Lemonade and FastFlowLM for the NPU in a Gentoo system
install.

Enabling the NPU makes Studio download a pinned FastFlowLM, either
directly (with flm_host.py standing in for lemond) or through Lemonade's
Ubuntu build in ~/.unsloth/studio/lemonade. With UNSLOTH_STUDIO_SYSTEM=1
(set by the unsloth-studio wrapper and by unsloth-desktop) it now runs
/usr/bin/lemond from sci-ml/lemonade, overridable with
UNSLOTH_STUDIO_LEMOND, and the installer reports a missing lemond or flm
as a package to emerge.

Since 2026.11.12 Studio itself can run a local FastFlowLM named by
UNSLOTH_FLM_NPU_BIN: it skips lemond's FastFlowLM install and the
pinned-version check, hands the binary to lemond as
LEMONADE_FLM_NPU_BIN, and validates the runtime through lemond's
/v1/system-info. In system mode that binary defaults to
/opt/fastflowlm/bin/flm from sci-ml/fastflowlm (UNSLOTH_STUDIO_FLM, the
override earlier Gentoo builds read, still applies). That default does
not count as a user-configured runtime when detecting hardware, so
machines without an NPU are not offered one.

